WEBVTT

00:00:11.750 --> 00:00:13.950
Oh, hey. It's Tatejima-san.

00:00:13.950 --> 00:00:16.320
Oh, Hatoya-san... Huh?!

00:00:16.740 --> 00:00:17.950
Heya.

00:00:18.500 --> 00:00:20.580
Y-You're carrying so much...

00:00:22.920 --> 00:00:24.490
H-Here, let me help you.

00:00:24.490 --> 00:00:26.030
Thanks.

00:00:26.030 --> 00:00:27.380
What is all this?

00:00:27.380 --> 00:00:31.770
Since we finally got a club room,
I wanted to make it a cozy space,

00:00:31.770 --> 00:00:34.510
so I brought a bunch of things from home.

00:00:35.240 --> 00:00:39.510
I brought a teapot, a 
cushion, and some snacks!

00:00:39.840 --> 00:00:42.230
<i>I-Is this her own room?</i>

00:00:52.150 --> 00:00:56.030
<b>Anima Yell!</b>

00:02:14.020 --> 00:02:15.530
Actually...

00:02:15.530 --> 00:02:17.820
I've even got a secret weapon.

00:02:18.090 --> 00:02:21.280
A secret weapon? That sounds menacing...

00:02:24.080 --> 00:02:27.330
As long as we have this, no one 
will be able to stand up again!

00:02:27.720 --> 00:02:29.830
It's a charming must-have!

00:02:30.520 --> 00:02:31.530
A desk?

00:02:31.530 --> 00:02:33.710
Nope! This is...

00:02:34.560 --> 00:02:36.120
A kotatsu!

00:02:36.120 --> 00:02:39.840
Would that still be "charming" in spring?

00:02:39.840 --> 00:02:42.850
<b>A/V Room</b>

00:02:41.110 --> 00:02:42.850
And we're here!

00:02:44.960 --> 00:02:46.810
Thanks for helping me!

00:02:46.810 --> 00:02:48.230
No problem.

00:02:48.670 --> 00:02:50.940
Why don't you stop in for a bit?

00:02:58.120 --> 00:03:00.490
Oh, actually, I...

00:03:00.490 --> 00:03:01.860
Oh, hey.

00:03:03.210 --> 00:03:04.450
Basketball-senpai!

00:03:04.780 --> 00:03:07.140
I wanted to ask a favor.

00:03:07.140 --> 00:03:09.230
And why are you calling me that?

00:03:09.230 --> 00:03:10.900
A favor...

00:03:12.660 --> 00:03:14.300
Do you need help asking someone out?

00:03:14.300 --> 00:03:17.090
Of course not! What are 
you even talking about?

00:03:19.490 --> 00:03:23.150
We're having a practice match 
with another school this Sunday,

00:03:23.150 --> 00:03:25.220
and we'd like you guys to cheer for us.

00:03:25.630 --> 00:03:29.000
Cheer?!

00:03:32.940 --> 00:03:37.070
<b>Episode 4: Let's Cheer UP!</b>

00:03:35.960 --> 00:03:39.070
Wow. So the captain came to see you?

00:03:39.070 --> 00:03:43.260
Yeah. Apparently, they're having 
a match at the municipal gym,

00:03:43.260 --> 00:03:44.950
so she wanted you guys to cheer for them.

00:03:45.510 --> 00:03:48.140
Thank you for delivering 
that message, Tatejima-san.

00:03:48.140 --> 00:03:50.950
Oh, no problem. More importantly...

00:03:52.220 --> 00:03:55.120
Do you think Hatoya-san will be okay?

00:03:55.120 --> 00:03:57.120
Oh, don't worry about her.

00:03:57.120 --> 00:03:59.900
She'll eventually wake up on her own.

00:03:59.900 --> 00:04:02.100
Well, I'll be going, then.

00:04:02.550 --> 00:04:04.420
Okay. Thanks again!

00:04:06.160 --> 00:04:07.580
Cheer?!

00:04:07.580 --> 00:04:08.720
You're finally awake.

00:04:08.720 --> 00:04:10.880
Basketball-senpai just asked us to—

00:04:10.880 --> 00:04:12.090
We already heard.

00:04:12.090 --> 00:04:14.840
What?! Did I tell you guys in my sleep?

00:04:21.430 --> 00:04:23.450
<i>The cheer association...</i>

00:04:23.450 --> 00:04:25.780
<i>It actually seems kind of fun.</i>

00:04:26.520 --> 00:04:29.330
<i>Wait! There's no way
I could be a cheerleader!</i>

00:04:33.750 --> 00:04:35.290
Did you see that?

00:04:36.080 --> 00:04:37.210
Yeah.

00:04:37.470 --> 00:04:41.360
That must mean she wants to be a 
cheerleader, but can't bring herself to say it!

00:04:41.360 --> 00:04:43.220
Tatejima-san!

00:04:42.080 --> 00:04:43.220
Hold it.

00:04:44.680 --> 00:04:47.280
If she can't say it, it probably means 
she's not confident about it.

00:04:47.280 --> 00:04:49.010
We shouldn't force the issue.

00:04:50.120 --> 00:04:52.040
And this is the perfect time for cheer!

00:04:52.040 --> 00:04:54.500
We can make her feel more self-confident!

00:04:56.260 --> 00:05:00.640
Then again, she can't cheer because 
she's not confident enough...

00:05:00.640 --> 00:05:03.740
But in order to boost her 
confidence, she needs cheer...

00:05:03.740 --> 00:05:06.110
And now you've made it a 
"chicken or the egg" scenario.

00:05:07.750 --> 00:05:08.890
In that case...

00:05:09.800 --> 00:05:13.070
Why don't we have her do a trial
membership before anyone decides?

00:05:13.070 --> 00:05:14.830
Yes, that! That's what I was trying to say!

00:05:14.830 --> 00:05:16.120
You liar!

00:05:25.670 --> 00:05:27.430
Huh? Is that a piano?

00:05:27.740 --> 00:05:33.180
H-H-Hey, didn't they say the cursed 
music room was on the floor beneath us?

00:05:33.180 --> 00:05:35.150
Cursed?

00:05:35.150 --> 00:05:38.250
But didn't they say that the piano 
sounds were only heard at night?

00:05:38.250 --> 00:05:40.220
Who cares about the minor details?

00:05:40.220 --> 00:05:41.980
K-Kohane, let's run!

00:05:41.980 --> 00:05:43.150
Perfect timing!

00:05:43.450 --> 00:05:45.180
I'm gonna go invite Ghostie, too!

00:05:45.180 --> 00:05:46.900
Not that way!

00:05:48.500 --> 00:05:51.340
Actually, if one of our members 
could play the piano,

00:05:51.340 --> 00:05:54.250
we could ask them to play 
some songs during practice.

00:05:54.250 --> 00:05:55.660
That's not it, either!

00:05:57.300 --> 00:05:58.320
Hello!

00:05:58.320 --> 00:06:00.130
Kohane...

00:06:01.330 --> 00:06:03.000
Huh? Are you by yourself?

00:06:03.000 --> 00:06:04.380
Y-Yes...

00:06:04.670 --> 00:06:06.360
Wait, is she possessed?

00:06:06.840 --> 00:06:08.800
Is that what's going on?

00:06:08.800 --> 00:06:11.850
Do you actually want the ghost to be here?

00:06:13.480 --> 00:06:14.850
Ghost?

00:06:15.320 --> 00:06:17.450
That's what people have been saying?

00:06:17.450 --> 00:06:21.370
So you were the piano ghost, Tatejima-san.

00:06:21.370 --> 00:06:22.110
Yes.

00:06:22.770 --> 00:06:25.710
I can't play too loudly at home,

00:06:25.710 --> 00:06:27.610
so when I mentioned it 
was hard to practice,

00:06:27.610 --> 00:06:30.510
my teacher said I could use this room.

00:06:30.510 --> 00:06:33.620
But people were saying they could 
hear the piano at night...

00:06:33.620 --> 00:06:36.330
I-I haven't been here at night, though.

00:06:37.200 --> 00:06:40.460
I'm assuming the rumors 
got a bit exaggerated.

00:06:40.460 --> 00:06:43.920
Yeah... I do play a bit after school, but...

00:06:43.920 --> 00:06:44.840
Um—

00:06:43.920 --> 00:06:45.590
Oh!

00:06:45.590 --> 00:06:47.550
So it wasn't true after all!

00:06:48.180 --> 00:06:50.410
You seem happy, Sawatari-san.

00:06:50.410 --> 00:06:54.300
I see. Anyway, we were wondering if you'd 
be interested in a trial membership.

00:06:54.640 --> 00:06:56.890
That was possibly the worst 
segue I've ever heard.

00:06:57.180 --> 00:07:01.100
Huh? Trial membership? You mean 
with the cheer association?

00:07:01.470 --> 00:07:02.640
Yeah!

00:07:02.640 --> 00:07:06.700
If you're not confident enough to 
officially join, but have some interest,

00:07:06.700 --> 00:07:08.440
we wanted you to at least give it a shot!

00:07:10.200 --> 00:07:11.680
Cheerleading is a lot of fun!

00:07:11.680 --> 00:07:13.950
It's good exercise, and it cheers you up!

00:07:14.350 --> 00:07:16.080
Okay, sure.

00:07:16.400 --> 00:07:17.660
That was super easy!

00:07:18.180 --> 00:07:20.170
I'll tell Kon-chan.

00:07:21.990 --> 00:07:24.790
Er, no... This wasn't a message.

00:07:25.200 --> 00:07:28.170
Akitsune-san already turned us down.

00:07:28.440 --> 00:07:30.470
I-I see...

00:07:30.870 --> 00:07:32.800
Wait, who were you trying to recruit, then?

00:07:33.430 --> 00:07:36.830
<i>Stare...</i>

00:07:36.830 --> 00:07:38.930
Wait, me?! I-I can't!

00:07:38.930 --> 00:07:39.930
Instant rejection!

00:07:39.930 --> 00:07:42.810
I-I-I mean... Cheerleading is embarrassing!

00:07:42.810 --> 00:07:44.270
<b>Embarrassing</b>

00:07:44.640 --> 00:07:46.270
N-No, I mean...

00:07:46.650 --> 00:07:50.280
<i>I'd</i> be embarrassed to 
cheer in front of people!

00:07:50.640 --> 00:07:54.330
I feel like I'd end up cursing people 
rather than cheering them up.

00:07:54.330 --> 00:07:56.630
Wait, did you just say "curse"?

00:07:57.520 --> 00:07:58.380
But...

00:07:59.130 --> 00:08:01.980
You play the piano, don't you?

00:08:01.980 --> 00:08:04.790
So aren't you accustomed to 
performing in front of people?

00:08:04.790 --> 00:08:06.720
I can't do that, either.

00:08:06.720 --> 00:08:08.600
I get really anxious,

00:08:08.600 --> 00:08:11.100
so when I play in front of people, 
I lose my composure...

00:08:13.130 --> 00:08:16.230
So... I'm sorry!

00:08:18.230 --> 00:08:20.750
Aw, that's too bad.

00:08:20.750 --> 00:08:24.440
Hatoya-san, I'm surprised 
you backed down so easily.

00:08:24.440 --> 00:08:27.400
Yeah! You were annoyingly 
persistent with me!

00:08:27.400 --> 00:08:31.040
W-Well, that's because we've 
been friends forever,

00:08:31.040 --> 00:08:32.650
so you're special.

00:08:33.070 --> 00:08:35.660
<i>Special... Special... Special...</i>

00:08:36.120 --> 00:08:39.660
Oh, you! I'm that special, eh?

00:08:41.660 --> 00:08:44.160
<b>A/V Room</b>

00:08:44.160 --> 00:08:46.960
It's unfortunate about Tatejima-san,

00:08:46.960 --> 00:08:49.580
but we need to start thinking about 
cheering for the basketball team.

00:08:49.580 --> 00:08:51.050
Oh, you're right!

00:08:51.050 --> 00:08:56.350
This time, let's concentrate on just 
cheering and not worry about any stunts.

00:08:56.350 --> 00:08:57.960
We haven't practiced enough, anyway.

00:08:57.960 --> 00:08:59.540
But, I mean...

00:09:00.460 --> 00:09:03.390
We can't even practice stunts 
in this room, anyway.

00:09:03.390 --> 00:09:04.700
The ceiling's too low.

00:09:04.700 --> 00:09:07.440
I wouldn't say it's impossible. 
Let's give it a shot!

00:09:07.770 --> 00:09:09.080
And go!

00:09:12.210 --> 00:09:14.060
This is what will happen.

00:09:14.060 --> 00:09:16.200
Then this room will end up cursed, too!

00:09:17.760 --> 00:09:21.630
We should be able to practice and learn 
a cheer routine if we start now,

00:09:21.630 --> 00:09:23.900
but the problem is acquiring our uniforms.

00:09:24.830 --> 00:09:27.820
Well, if we just wore 
T-shirts and pleated skirts,

00:09:27.820 --> 00:09:29.320
it might <i>look</i> like uniforms...

00:09:29.320 --> 00:09:29.920
No!

00:09:36.270 --> 00:09:39.070
We're going to be cheering in 
front of a crowd for the first time,

00:09:39.070 --> 00:09:41.420
so I'd like to at least have uniforms.

00:09:41.420 --> 00:09:45.610
Well, here's an online retailer.
This is what they'd cost.

00:09:49.880 --> 00:09:52.460
Th-That's pretty, uh...

00:09:52.460 --> 00:09:55.460
That's much higher than I expected...

00:09:56.390 --> 00:09:57.570
Um...

00:09:58.340 --> 00:10:01.200
If you think it'll be difficult 
for you to prepare uniforms...

00:10:01.200 --> 00:10:04.000
If you don't mind, I'll bring 
my uniforms from middle school.

00:10:04.000 --> 00:10:06.520
The colors and designs won't match, but...

00:10:07.520 --> 00:10:08.250
No!

00:10:08.670 --> 00:10:10.720
We should all match!

00:10:10.720 --> 00:10:12.670
I appreciate the offer, though.

00:10:12.670 --> 00:10:14.760
Yeah. I mean, we're a team.

00:10:15.040 --> 00:10:17.130
I-I see...

00:10:17.130 --> 00:10:21.390
Besides, if we can't buy the 
cuckoo, we shall make one!

00:10:21.720 --> 00:10:22.760
We're making a bird?!

00:10:22.760 --> 00:10:26.300
Let's just go with "if we can't 
buy uniforms, let's make them."

00:10:26.300 --> 00:10:28.410
Arima-san actually took you seriously.

00:10:28.410 --> 00:10:30.600
I see... Homemade...

00:10:30.600 --> 00:10:33.150
We still have some time 
before the practice match.

00:10:33.990 --> 00:10:35.370
I did a bit of searching,

00:10:35.370 --> 00:10:37.930
and there were some sites 
that had some patterns.

00:10:37.930 --> 00:10:38.860
Like this one.

00:10:40.010 --> 00:10:40.860
I see...

00:10:41.360 --> 00:10:43.320
Now all we need is a sewing machine.

00:10:44.520 --> 00:10:46.980
Can either of you sew?

00:10:49.280 --> 00:10:52.000
I can't believe my flawless 
plan had a flaw in it!

00:10:52.000 --> 00:10:55.000
I've only ever made an 
apron in home ec before.

00:10:55.000 --> 00:10:56.510
Likewise.

00:10:56.510 --> 00:10:59.050
I guess sewing them ourselves 
would be a bit hard.

00:10:59.050 --> 00:11:01.270
No, it'll be fine.

00:11:01.270 --> 00:11:04.990
They didn't even have sewing machines 
years ago, so if we consider that...

00:11:04.990 --> 00:11:06.640
I mean, you're not wrong...

00:11:06.640 --> 00:11:08.140
Well, even with light...

00:11:08.520 --> 00:11:09.900
We only need candles!

00:11:09.900 --> 00:11:12.650
We don't need to abandon 
modern civilization <i>that</i> much!

00:11:13.070 --> 00:11:16.640
Okay, let's try making patterns ourselves

00:11:16.640 --> 00:11:18.860
by looking at the samples on the internet.

00:11:20.320 --> 00:11:24.560
But to think that the ghost 
was actually Tatejima-san...

00:11:24.560 --> 00:11:27.830
Aren't you glad there wasn't 
actually a ghost, Uki?

00:11:28.140 --> 00:11:31.120
I-I-It's not like I can't handle ghosts...

00:11:31.120 --> 00:11:34.830
As a matter of fact, I have no interest...

00:11:34.830 --> 00:11:36.500
in ghosts!

00:11:38.550 --> 00:11:40.630
You actually like them, don't you?

00:11:43.220 --> 00:11:47.010
Kaminoki Municipal Gymnasium

00:11:47.010 --> 00:11:48.970
Today's finally the day!

00:11:49.860 --> 00:11:52.240
I'm so nervous, my stomach's starting to hurt.

00:11:52.240 --> 00:11:54.910
We'll be fine, as long as we 
do exactly what we practiced.

00:11:54.910 --> 00:11:56.460
Let's relax.

00:11:56.460 --> 00:11:59.040
Yeah, yeah! Relax, relax!

00:11:59.040 --> 00:12:02.280
I think you actually need to be 
a bit more nervous, Kohane.

00:12:02.280 --> 00:12:07.080
<i>One, two, three, four, 
five, six, seven, eight.</i>

00:12:05.380 --> 00:12:09.290
Looks like the basketball 
team is already warming up.

00:12:07.080 --> 00:12:11.310
Two, two, three, four, 
five, six, seven, eight...

00:12:10.450 --> 00:12:13.540
Basketball-senpai! 
Thanks for having us today!

00:12:11.310 --> 00:12:12.680
Next...

00:12:13.540 --> 00:12:14.790
Huh?

00:12:14.790 --> 00:12:17.920
And now all the second- and 
third-years are staring at us.

00:12:17.920 --> 00:12:20.420
<b>Girls' Changing Room</b>

00:12:37.140 --> 00:12:39.440
Thank goodness we finished 
the uniforms in time!

00:12:39.440 --> 00:12:42.940
By the way, Hatoya-san, 
why did you bring this big bag?

00:12:44.570 --> 00:12:45.990
Well, you see...

00:12:47.560 --> 00:12:48.950
Ta-da!

00:12:49.780 --> 00:12:51.500
I made lots!

00:12:52.700 --> 00:12:55.520
Are these for the crowd?

00:12:55.520 --> 00:12:56.370
Yup!

00:12:56.780 --> 00:12:59.880
I thought they would make 
the cheers even better!

00:13:01.080 --> 00:13:03.130
Wow...

00:13:04.400 --> 00:13:06.860
I can tell exactly what 
order you made them in.

00:13:06.860 --> 00:13:08.260
Yeah, so can I...

00:13:08.690 --> 00:13:10.860
We would've helped if you'd asked.

00:13:10.860 --> 00:13:13.280
I thought about it at the last minute.

00:13:13.280 --> 00:13:16.270
Oh, I gave Tatejima-san hers at school.

00:13:18.730 --> 00:13:20.150
Are you sure I can have these?

00:13:20.150 --> 00:13:23.910
Yeah! You should come cheer 
them on if you can, too.

00:13:24.610 --> 00:13:27.580
I made a call chart.

00:13:28.050 --> 00:13:31.160
It lists all the calls we'll be doing today.

00:13:31.160 --> 00:13:33.460
I followed Sawatari-san's advice.

00:13:33.460 --> 00:13:34.370
Right?

00:13:35.760 --> 00:13:36.940
Sawatari-san?

00:13:36.940 --> 00:13:39.000
Huh? Oh, sorry...

00:13:41.080 --> 00:13:42.500
I just got a really good idea!

00:13:42.800 --> 00:13:47.380
Hey, how about if we do this?

00:13:43.840 --> 00:13:47.380
<i>I'm not exactly sure why, but
I have a bad feeling about this...</i>

00:13:54.120 --> 00:13:56.890
<i>Am I allowed to come in?</i>

00:13:57.560 --> 00:13:59.400
They asked that we pass these around.

00:13:59.400 --> 00:14:00.940
Wow, pom poms?

00:14:00.940 --> 00:14:02.920
Are we supposed to cheer with these?

00:14:06.200 --> 00:14:07.900
<i>It's Hatoya-san and the others.</i>

00:14:09.640 --> 00:14:11.610
<i>Their uniforms are so cute!</i>

00:14:11.610 --> 00:14:13.410
<i>Maybe I do want to try one on...</i>

00:14:20.440 --> 00:14:22.700
Wings that fly through the big, blue sky!

00:14:23.550 --> 00:14:25.160
Hatoya Kohane!

00:14:25.920 --> 00:14:28.470
The gale that gallops across the land!

00:14:29.270 --> 00:14:31.140
Arima Hizume!

00:14:31.930 --> 00:14:35.820
Um... The sage of the forest! Sawatari Uki!

00:14:35.820 --> 00:14:36.680
Huh?!

00:14:36.680 --> 00:14:38.810
Wait! You're talking about gorillas!

00:14:40.310 --> 00:14:42.700
We're the Kaminoki High 
School Cheer Association!

00:14:42.700 --> 00:14:45.280
Thanks for having us today!

00:14:47.880 --> 00:14:51.660
<i>Nope! I definitely wouldn't 
be able to do that...</i>

00:14:52.550 --> 00:14:54.880
Looks like our introductions went well!

00:14:54.880 --> 00:14:57.290
Though that's not at all how I imagined them...

00:14:57.290 --> 00:14:59.290
Good idea, my ass!

00:14:59.760 --> 00:15:01.790
That was so embarrassing...

00:15:02.280 --> 00:15:04.010
But we livened up the crowd!

00:15:04.010 --> 00:15:06.120
You mean we scared them!

00:15:06.120 --> 00:15:07.050
Maybe!

00:15:11.110 --> 00:15:13.640
Thanks... I'm not as nervous now.

00:15:13.640 --> 00:15:14.890
No prob.

00:15:19.560 --> 00:15:21.560
Tatejima-san!

00:15:25.190 --> 00:15:26.070
<b>Thank</b>

00:15:26.070 --> 00:15:27.190
<b>you</b>

00:15:27.190 --> 00:15:27.820
<b>for</b>

00:15:27.820 --> 00:15:28.570
<b>coming</b>

00:15:28.990 --> 00:15:30.910
Is that what cheerleading's 
supposed to look like?

00:15:30.910 --> 00:15:32.440
She's doing some strange movements...

00:15:32.440 --> 00:15:34.170
Was that like semaphore flag signaling?

00:15:34.170 --> 00:15:36.870
<i>I-I'm so sorry, Hatoya-san!</i>

00:15:45.560 --> 00:15:47.630
Okay, here we go!

00:15:47.630 --> 00:15:49.930
Go, go, Kaminoki!

00:15:49.930 --> 00:15:51.680
Let's go, Kaminoki!

00:15:51.680 --> 00:15:53.050
Go, fight, win!

00:15:53.050 --> 00:16:08.150
Go! Go! Go!

00:16:06.520 --> 00:16:08.150
<i>Who in the world is that?!</i>

00:16:11.570 --> 00:16:14.760
<i>So this is what cheer's like.</i>

00:16:16.040 --> 00:16:19.660
<i>It's full of energy, it's cute...</i>

00:16:21.170 --> 00:16:23.740
<i>and definitely something I can't do.</i>

00:16:25.350 --> 00:16:27.170
Hey, look!

00:16:27.170 --> 00:16:30.840
Don't their uniforms look 
homemade? They're so cute!

00:16:30.840 --> 00:16:32.840
Right? I wanna wear one, too.

00:16:33.200 --> 00:16:34.520
<i>Yup, yup...</i>

00:16:35.890 --> 00:16:38.650
<i>No, no, no! I can't!</i>

00:16:49.270 --> 00:16:51.280
<b>Yashirogaoka                                   Kaminoki</b>

00:16:58.070 --> 00:17:00.960
Oh, no. The other team scored again.

00:17:00.960 --> 00:17:03.540
Now they're eight points ahead.

00:17:04.260 --> 00:17:07.760
This is exactly when we're supposed
to shout and liven things up!

00:17:07.760 --> 00:17:09.690
Um...

00:17:09.690 --> 00:17:12.050
How would I say "moriage" in English?

00:17:12.550 --> 00:17:15.210
Mori! Age! Yo!

00:17:15.210 --> 00:17:16.050
"Yo"?!

00:17:18.000 --> 00:17:21.080
I think "moriagaru" is "cheer up" in English.

00:17:21.080 --> 00:17:22.240
Huh?

00:17:22.240 --> 00:17:24.600
What the heck? That sounds so cool!

00:17:25.250 --> 00:17:28.060
Let's cheer up! Let's cheer up!

00:17:28.060 --> 00:17:31.320
Let's cheer up! Let's cheer up!

00:17:31.320 --> 00:17:44.330
Let's cheer up! Let's cheer up!

00:17:36.640 --> 00:17:37.820
I see.

00:17:39.780 --> 00:17:42.510
You don't do cheer alone...

00:17:42.510 --> 00:17:43.720
You do it together.

00:17:44.330 --> 00:17:47.580
Let's cheer up! Let's cheer up!

00:17:47.580 --> 00:17:50.590
Let's go, Kaminoki! Go for win!

00:17:50.590 --> 00:17:53.590
Let's go, Kaminoki! Go for win!

00:17:53.590 --> 00:17:56.840
Let's cheer up! Let's cheer up!

00:17:56.840 --> 00:17:59.840
Let's go, Kaminoki! Go for win!

00:17:59.840 --> 00:18:10.890
Let's cheer up! Let's cheer up!

00:18:10.890 --> 00:18:14.000
Let's go, Kaminoki! Go for win!

00:18:14.000 --> 00:18:16.860
Let's cheer up! Let's cheer up!

00:18:16.860 --> 00:18:19.860
Let's go, Kaminoki! Go for win!

00:18:19.860 --> 00:18:23.280
Let's go, Kaminoki! Go for win!

00:18:21.620 --> 00:18:24.510
What's wrong, Kana? You're spacing out.

00:18:23.280 --> 00:18:26.410
Let's cheer up! Let's cheer up!

00:18:24.510 --> 00:18:25.900
Do you not feel well?

00:18:25.900 --> 00:18:27.640
Huh? Oh, it's nothing.

00:18:26.410 --> 00:18:29.620
Let's go, Kaminoki! Go for win!

00:18:27.640 --> 00:18:28.810
I'm fine.

00:18:29.620 --> 00:18:32.710
<i>You could be so much more amazing than this.</i>

00:18:29.620 --> 00:18:33.380
Let's cheer up! Let's cheer up!

00:18:33.380 --> 00:18:35.880
Let's cheer up! Let's cheer up!

00:18:33.380 --> 00:18:35.880
<b>Yashirogaoka               Kaminoki</b>

00:18:35.880 --> 00:18:38.880
Let's cheer up! Let's cheer up!

00:18:38.880 --> 00:18:42.100
Let's go, Kaminoki! Go for win!

00:18:50.270 --> 00:18:52.010
It went in!

00:18:52.010 --> 00:18:53.820
They turned it around!

00:18:53.820 --> 00:18:56.140
Yay!

00:18:56.820 --> 00:18:59.240
<i>I got totally caught up 
before I realized it...</i>

00:18:59.240 --> 00:19:01.360
Basketball-senpai!

00:19:01.360 --> 00:19:02.240
Kohane!

00:19:04.240 --> 00:19:05.660
<b>Yashirogaoka                                                     Kaminoki</b>

00:19:04.240 --> 00:19:07.290
We did it!

00:19:09.320 --> 00:19:11.080
<i>She's more acrobatic than I thought!</i>

00:19:22.590 --> 00:19:25.470
Kaminoki Municipal Gymnasium

00:19:32.500 --> 00:19:34.000
Thanks for all you did today.

00:19:34.000 --> 00:19:35.640
No, thank you!

00:19:35.640 --> 00:19:37.450
Thank you very much.

00:19:37.450 --> 00:19:38.780
Oh, no, really.

00:19:40.070 --> 00:19:41.840
Seriously, good work.

00:19:41.840 --> 00:19:44.240
Yeah, uh... Don't worry about her.

00:19:45.380 --> 00:19:47.370
But I have to admit, 
cheerleading's pretty great.

00:19:47.370 --> 00:19:49.200
You guys gave us the push we needed.

00:19:49.600 --> 00:19:50.730
Thanks.

00:19:51.750 --> 00:19:54.650
No, no, thank you!

00:19:54.650 --> 00:19:57.130
<i>Her cheer power was 
immediately replenished.</i>

00:19:58.870 --> 00:20:00.550
U-Um...

00:20:00.940 --> 00:20:02.920
Oh, Tatejima-san!

00:20:02.920 --> 00:20:05.420
Anyway, thanks again, you guys.

00:20:05.420 --> 00:20:07.060
Great work!

00:20:07.470 --> 00:20:09.560
Tatejima-san, did you see us?

00:20:09.840 --> 00:20:11.070
Yeah!

00:20:11.070 --> 00:20:13.220
Cheer's amazing.

00:20:13.220 --> 00:20:16.250
Though I don't think I'd 
ever be able to do it.

00:20:18.310 --> 00:20:23.070
<i>I still don't think I can be as sparkly 
as they are when they're cheering.</i>

00:20:31.260 --> 00:20:32.650
<i>But maybe together...</i>

00:20:39.920 --> 00:20:43.170
But I still want to try 
cheerleading with you!

00:20:46.680 --> 00:20:48.620
You'll be fine, Tatejima-san!

00:20:48.620 --> 00:20:50.300
Here's the club application!

00:20:50.300 --> 00:20:51.430
Where were you hiding that?!

00:20:51.520 --> 00:20:52.930
<b>Club Application
Club name (Association name)
Class | Name</b>

00:20:54.360 --> 00:20:56.190
Huh? M-My name?

00:20:56.190 --> 00:20:59.080
Put anything. You could use 
a pen name or even a fake one!

00:20:59.080 --> 00:21:00.120
No, she can't.

00:21:00.440 --> 00:21:03.700
<b>Club Application
Club name (Association name)
Cheer Association
Class | Name
1-2 | Tatejima Kotetsu</b>

00:21:01.750 --> 00:21:03.700
Tatejima Kotetsu-chan...

00:21:04.030 --> 00:21:05.530
You sound so strong!

00:21:05.530 --> 00:21:07.690
There's a famous sword that shares your name.

00:21:07.690 --> 00:21:10.440
The one that the commander 
of the Shinsengumi used...

00:21:12.200 --> 00:21:14.680
I don't really like it.

00:21:14.680 --> 00:21:16.990
That name is way stronger than I am,

00:21:16.990 --> 00:21:19.710
and it's not even a girl's name.

00:21:19.710 --> 00:21:22.140
W-Well, I mean, it sounds cool!

00:21:22.140 --> 00:21:23.640
I like it.

00:21:23.640 --> 00:21:25.240
It sounds delicious!

00:21:25.240 --> 00:21:27.290
<i>Are they trying to cheer me up?</i>

00:21:27.720 --> 00:21:30.720
<b>Kaminoki Municipal Gymnasium</b>

00:21:31.670 --> 00:21:33.130
What the heck was that?

00:21:33.130 --> 00:21:35.200
It was so much fun!

00:21:35.200 --> 00:21:39.240
<i>To be honest, I'm still not very confident.</i>

00:21:39.240 --> 00:21:43.580
<i>But I think I might just make it, as long 
as I'm with Hatoya-san and the others.</i>

00:21:43.990 --> 00:21:47.400
Now if we can just get one more person 
to join, we'll be promoted to a club!

00:21:47.400 --> 00:21:48.680
Just a little more!

00:21:48.680 --> 00:21:52.390
Yes. I'll do whatever I can to help.

00:23:27.560 --> 00:23:28.970
High V! Low V!

00:23:28.970 --> 00:23:30.860
Can I really do this?

00:23:30.860 --> 00:23:32.430
I'll teach you everything you need to know.

00:23:32.430 --> 00:23:34.640
I'm happy, nervous, and excited!

00:23:34.640 --> 00:23:37.210
Next time on episode 5 of <i>Anima Yell!</i>

00:23:37.210 --> 00:23:38.890
"Arm Motions With a Smile."

00:23:38.890 --> 00:23:40.350
All together now!

00:23:40.350 --> 00:23:41.980
High V! Low V!
